# Edge cache for the prerendered HTML routes.
#
# Why this file exists: Cloudflare Workers static assets send
#   Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
# on every HTML file. Measured on 2026-11-07: six consecutive requests for /
# all came back cf-cache-status: REVALIDATED, never HIT. The file itself is
# static, but every single visit still paid an edge -> origin hop for it, and
# that hop sits in front of first paint for every visitor.
#
# s-maxage is honoured by shared caches (Cloudflare) and ignored by browsers,
# so max-age=0 keeps the owner's rule intact: a browser still revalidates every
# time, so a redeploy is visible on refresh immediately. Only the edge gets a
# 60-second lease. Worst case after a deploy: some nodes serve the previous HTML
# for up to 60s.
#
# Rules are listed per path on purpose. _headers merges every matching rule and
# joins duplicate header values with a comma, so a /* rule would corrupt the
# 1-year immutable Cache-Control that /_astro/* fingerprints rely on.
#
# Only prerendered routes belong here. SSR routes (products, blog, categories,
# videos, about, project-gallery) are generated by the Worker, and _headers does
# not apply to Worker-generated responses at all - they keep revalidating, which
# is what makes database edits show up on refresh.
#
# Regenerate this list after adding a static page:
#   Get-ChildItem dist\client -Recurse -Filter *.html
#
# Comments are English because this file ships into dist/client.

/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, s-maxage=60
/404.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, s-maxage=60
